content.text:
I’ve revised the [proposal](/Users/cooper/Projects/taxkit/docs/product-specs/common-practice-foundation-review.md) and removed the 12 new audit-packet files.

- Keep Website RPC while adopting Common Practice’s clients that check inputs, replies and errors. :codex-annotation{index="1"}
- Put Cloudflare first. Keep Bun supported, with shared packages independent of either host. :codex-annotation{index="2"}
- Target **zero Alchemy patches**: declare the API before the Website and handle `www` redirects in the Website, including static files. :codex-annotation{index="3"}

The plan now copies Common Practice’s ordinary commits, PRs, Actions, native Alchemy and Doppler. It removes extra approval files, receipt workflows, historical qualification checks and the custom release runner. Tests of tax answers, API behaviour and package installation stay.

This completes the revised design; the code changes remain pending. Docs checks passed. Full verification stopped on temporary-file permission errors.

